    "created_at": "2026-11-15T14:17:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T14:17:28Z",
    "body": "Decision: control-side G41/G42 H offsets and skim passes that reuse one part path remain unsupported in the Sodick post.\n\nThe document stores no H-register identifiers or values. The wire laws judge generated wire-centre paths from the conditions' wire radius and spark gap. They cannot certify an offset chosen separately at the control. The milling compensation contract does not establish Sodick's engage and cancel geometry. No H number format is adopted because no H word is emitted.\n\nThe patch gives every COMP request a Sodick refusal that names the operation and suppresses its later cuts. COMP OFF cannot clear that refusal. The next plain section still posts. The existing engine warning already blocked app output; the patch makes the reason specific and suppresses affected cutting blocks in diagnostic output. The existing skim refusal stays in place.\n\nFuture support needs sourced H format and units, stored per-pass values, a proof that the programmed path produces the centre path judged by the wire laws, revalidation when values change, a rough-plus-skim golden, and a gouge refusal test.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
